      "Trophic Food Chains and Eltonian Ecological Pyramids: Grazing food chains (initiated by living green plants consumed by herbivores) versus Detritus food chains (initiated by dead organic matter, decaying leaf litter, and saprotrophic microorganisms); Interconnected food webs conferring ecosystem resilience; Ecological pyramids: Pyramid of numbers, Pyramid of biomass (inverted in marine pelagic plankton communities), and Pyramid of energy (strictly upright across all ecosystems).",
      "Primary and Secondary Ecosystem Productivity: Quantitative metrics of biological synthesis: Gross Primary Productivity (GPP: total rate of photosynthetic solar energy capture); Net Primary Productivity (NPP: biomass remaining after autotrophic respiratory losses: NPP equals GPP minus autotrophic respiration); Secondary productivity (rate of biomass synthesis by heterotrophic consumers); High productivity ecosystems (tropical rainforests, coral reefs, estuaries) versus low productivity ecosystems (deserts, open ocean gyres).",
      "Biogeochemical Cycling of Essential Nutrients: Gaseous biogeochemical cycles (carbon and nitrogen cycles with global atmospheric reservoirs) versus Sedimentary biogeochemical cycles (phosphorus and sulfur cycles with slow lithospheric rock reservoirs); Biological nitrogen cycle: Atmospheric N2 fixation (Rhizobium, Azotobacter), nitrification (Nitrosomonas, Nitrobacter), plant nitrate assimilation, ammonification, and anaerobic denitrification (Pseudomonas) closing the cycle.",
