      "Mathematical Formulations of Population Growth: Exponential growth model in unconstrained environments: Rate of change dN/dt equals r multiplied by N, yielding a characteristic J-shaped curve; Intrinsic rate of natural increase (r); Logistic growth model in resource-constrained environments: Rate of change dN/dt equals rN multiplied by (1 minus N/K), yielding a sigmoid S-shaped curve governed by environmental carrying capacity (K).",
      "Community Ecology and Interspecific Species Interactions: Positive symbioses: Mutualism (obligate cooperation, e.g., mycorrhizae, lichens) and Commensalism (one benefits, other unaffected, e.g., epiphytic orchids on trees); Negative interactions: Predation, Parasitism (endo- and ectoparasites), Competition (intra- and interspecific), and Amensalism (one inhibited, other unaffected, e.g., Penicillium antibiotic secretion); Gause competitive exclusion principle and resource partitioning.",
      "Ecological Succession (Hydrosere and Xerosere): Orderly, predictable directional replacement of biotic communities over ecological time: Primary succession (initiating on newly exposed sterile substrates lacking soil) versus Secondary succession (initiating on disturbed areas with pre-existing soil seed banks); Autogenic versus allogenic succession; Hydrosere stages (phytoplankton, submerged, rooted floating, reed swamp, marsh meadow, woodland, climax forest); Xerosere stages (crustose lichen, foliose lichen, moss, herb, shrub, forest climax).",
      "Threats to Global Biodiversity and Conservation Strategies: Anthropogenic pressures driving the Holocene Sixth Mass Extinction: Habitat fragmentation and destruction, over-exploitation, poaching, environmental pollution, climate change, and invasive alien species (Lantana camara, Parthenium hysterophorus, Eichhornia crassipes); In situ conservation (Protected Area Network: National Parks, Wildlife Sanctuaries, Biosphere Reserves) and Ex situ conservation (Botanical Gardens, Zoological Parks, Seed Banks, Cryopreservation)."
