      "Air Pollution Causes and Primary Pollutants: Release of toxic combustion gases and particulate emissions into troposphere: Carbon monoxide (CO: incomplete combustion, binds hemoglobin to form carboxyhemoglobin causing asphyxiation), Sulfur dioxide (SO2: coal combustion, respiratory irritant), Nitrogen oxides (NOx: high-temperature vehicle combustion), Particulate Matter (PM10 and fine inhalable PM2.5 penetrating deep pulmonary alveoli).",
      "Secondary Air Pollutants and Photochemical Smog: Chemical transformations in ambient air catalyzed by sunlight: Photochemical smog formed by reaction of volatile organic compounds (VOCs) and nitrogen oxides in presence of UV light, generating toxic tropospheric ozone, aldehydes, and peroxyacetyl nitrate (PAN); Classical London sulfurous smog (SO2 and coal soot in humid cold air); Acid rain (sulfuric acid and nitric acid precipitation at pH < 5.6 leaching toxic aluminum from soils).",
      "Air Pollution Industrial Control Technologies: Particulate emission reduction devices: Gravitational settling chambers, cyclone centrifugal separators, fabric baghouse filters (cloth filter bags trapping fine dusts with 99% efficiency), and Electrostatic Precipitators (ESP: high-voltage corona discharge ionizing particulates collected on grounded plates); Gaseous emission control: Wet scrubbers using limestone slurries to capture SO2 (flue-gas desulfurization).",
      "Water Pollution Mechanisms and Eutrophication: Contamination by domestic sewage, agricultural runoff (synthetic fertilizers, pesticides), and toxic industrial discharges; Cultural Eutrophication: Excess nitrogen and phosphorus inputs trigger massive algal blooms, blocking sunlight, decaying upon death, and causing bacterial oxygen depletion, resulting in aquatic hypoxia, dead zones, and massive fish kills.",
      "Biochemical Oxygen Demand (BOD) and Chemical Oxygen Demand (COD): Water quality monitoring parameters: Biochemical Oxygen Demand (BOD5: quantity of dissolved oxygen consumed by aerobic microorganisms to decompose organic matter over 5 days at 20 degrees Celsius; clean water BOD < 2 mg/L, raw sewage BOD > 300 mg/L); Chemical Oxygen Demand (COD: quantity of oxygen consumed to chemically oxidize all organic compounds using boiling potassium dichromate in acid; COD is always higher than BOD).",
      "Wastewater Treatment Plant Engineering: Modern three-stage municipal sewage treatment: Primary treatment (physical mechanical screening, grit removal, sedimentation tanks removing settleable suspended solids); Secondary treatment (biological aeration tanks where aerobic activated sludge flocs oxidize dissolved organic matter, followed by secondary clarifiers); Tertiary advanced treatment (sand filtration, nutrient removal, chlorination or UV disinfection).",
      "Noise Pollution Dynamics and Acoustic Barriers: Unwanted, damaging sound vibrations: Measured on logarithmic decibel (dB) scale; Permissible ambient day/night limits (Industrial: 75/70 dB; Residential: 55/45 dB; Silence zones near hospitals: 50/40 dB); Health impacts: Permanent sensorineural hearing threshold shift, tinnitus, elevated blood pressure, hypertension, sleep disruption; Control via green belts (vegetation buffer rows) and soundproofing acoustic baffles.",
