      "Multidimensional Values of Biodiversity: Anthropocentric and ecocentric valuations: Consumptive use value (direct harvesting for food, fuel wood, fodder, and traditional medicinal plants); Productive use value (commercial timber, pharmaceuticals, industrial oils, agricultural crops); Social and cultural values (sacred groves, religious reverence); Ethical and intrinsic values (inherent right of all species to exist); Option values (potential future discoveries of drugs and genetic traits); Ecosystem services (pollination, flood control, carbon sequestration).",
      "India as a Mega-Diversity Nation: India is one of the 17 recognized megadiverse nations of the world; Occupying only 2.4 percent of global land area while harboring over 7 to 8 percent of all recorded global species; Rich botanical wealth (over 47000 plant species) and faunal diversity (over 90000 animal species), supported by diverse biomes ranging from alpine glaciers to tropical rainforests and coral reefs.",
