      "Environmental Ethics and Public Environmental Movements: Philosophical attitudes toward nature: Anthropocentrism (human-centered utility) versus Ecocentrism (nature-centered intrinsic value); Grassroots environmental movements in India: Chipko Movement (1973 in Uttarakhand: villagers hugging trees to prevent commercial logging), Appiko Movement (Karnataka), Silent Valley Movement (Kerala: preserving tropical rainforest from hydroelectric dam), and Narmada Bachao Andolan (social movement against large dam displacement).",
